/-
# Generators of 2-groups and ranks of abelian subgroups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 4.61)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.61 (S. A. Syskin): does there exist a
linear function `f` with the following property: if every abelian subgroup of a finite `2`-group `G`
is generated by `n` elements, then `G` is generated by `f(n)` elements?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Schreier

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.TwoGroupAbelianRankLinearBoundKourovka4Problem61Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.61 (S. A.
Syskin). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700268 (`KOU-4.61`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A linear function is `f(n) = an + b`; natural coefficients suffice, since a real linear bound is
dominated by `⌈a⌉n + ⌈b⌉` on `ℕ`. "Generated by `n` elements" is `Group.rank ≤ n` (Mathlib's least
size of a generating set); a finite `2`-group is a finite group with `IsPGroup 2`.
-/

/-- Kourovka 4.61 (S. A. Syskin): there is a linear function `f(n) = a n + b` such that every
finite `2`-group all of whose abelian subgroups are generated by `n` elements is generated by
`f(n)` elements. The number of generators is Mathlib's `Group.rank` (the least size of a
generating set); natural coefficients suffice, since a real linear bound is dominated by one with
coefficients `⌈a⌉`, `⌈b⌉`. -/
def existsLinearGeneratorBoundTwoGroups : Prop :=
  ∃ a b : ℕ, ∀ (n : ℕ) (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G], IsPGroup 2 G →
    (∀ A : Subgroup G, (∀ x ∈ A, ∀ y ∈ A, x * y = y * x) → Group.rank A ≤ n) →
    Group.rank G ≤ a * n + b

/--
Resolved false: Ol'shanskiĭ shows that the number of generators of a finite `2`-group is not bounded
by a linear function of the maximal number of generators of its abelian subgroups; the Kourovka
Archive answers 4.61 "No". Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in
Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved
Problems, Problem 4.61 (S. A. Syskin); resolution: A. Yu. Ol'shanskiĭ, The number of generators and
orders of abelian subgroups of finite p-groups, Math. Notes 23 (1978), 183-185, Kourovka Archive of
Solved Problems, Problem 4.61: No, https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01651428.
-/
public theorem_wanted existsLinearGeneratorBoundTwoGroups_refuted :
    ¬ existsLinearGeneratorBoundTwoGroups

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.TwoGroupAbelianRankLinearBoundKourovka4Problem61Wanted
